art of speech":"PROPN","personal data":"none","postal addresses":"none","source":"pile-uncopyrighted","toxicity":"none"},"text":"'Esquire U.K.' Joins the Deen Parade\n\nHOLLYWOOD—As the opening of his debut mainstream vehicle, The Canyons, approaches, James Deen gets yet another profile in a major periodical, this time the U.K. edition of men's interest magazine Esquire.\n\nDubbing Deen \"the Ryan Gosling of porn\" (wait, we thought that was Richie Calhoun), the piece by Sanjiv Bhattacharya relays the usual tales of Deen's upbringing, his single-minded pursuit of a porn career, his selection for the role of Christian in The Canyons and some rumination as to whether he may be a sex addict.\n\nADVERTISEMENT\n\nIt also details two porn shoots employing Deen—the first being AMKingdom's forthcoming epic Saving Humanity, which pairs him with Tara Lynn Foxx (whose age the story pegs in different spots as both 22 and 23 ... the latter is correct); and the second being an unnamed Digital Playground production placing him opposite girlfriend Stoya (the director of which, Robby D., gets name-checked in the piece with the misspelling \"Robbie D\").\n\nThe profile also touches on Deen's multiple crownings at the AVN Awards as Male Performer of the Year—though it incorrectly states that he's won the trophy thrice, in 2009, 2010 and 2013; in 2010, he won ... nothing.","tokens":["'","Es","quire"," U",".","K",".'"," Jo","ins"," the"," De","en"," Par","ade","\n","\n","HO","LLY","WO","OD","—","As"," the"," opening"," of"," his"," debut"," mainstream"," vehicle",","," The"," C","any","ons",","," approaches",","," James"," De","en"," gets"," yet"," another"," profile"," in"," a"," major"," period","ical",","," this"," time"," the"," U",".","K","."," edition"," of"," men","'s"," interest"," magazine"," Es","quire",".","\n","\n","D","ub","bing"," De","en"," \"","the"," Ryan"," Gos","ling"," of"," porn","\""," (","wait",","," we"," thought"," that"," was"," Rich","ie"," Cal","h","oun","),"